WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.547
EXTRACT and DATE_TRUNC solve different problems.

00:00:03.547 --> 00:00:07.397
EXTRACT month gives a number such as three.

00:00:07.397 --> 00:00:13.467
DATE_TRUNC month gives a full month bucket such as March first, twenty twenty-six at midnight.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:21.112
If you group only by month number, March from multiple years can be combined accidentally.

00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:27.152
DATE_TRUNC often gives a safer full-period key for time-series aggregation.

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:30.412
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:33.702
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:33.702 --> 00:00:38.502
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:38.502 --> 00:00:45.347
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:45.347 --> 00:00:47.127
daylight-saving changes.
